-- title:
--   Supersingular places injectively indexed by Γ₀(M')-moduli points
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`.
--
--   **Global data over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$.** A prime $q$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. A valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ such that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`LiesOverPrime`); write $\kappa$ for the residue field of $A$. A finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M' = \kappa(\mathrm{jqModC}\,\kappa,\ \mathrm{jqNModC}\,\kappa\,M')$ over $\kappa$ which, by `hW`, consists precisely of the places satisfying the predicate `IsSupersingularPlace q M' κ` (the members of `ssPlaces q M' κ`), and a distinguished element $s \in W$. The hypothesis `hle` states that `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\bar{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\bar{\mathbb Q}((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field over $\mathbb Q$, is contained in `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2 * M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$.
--
--   **Reduction datum.** A `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ for $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$: that is, a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of the source, a surjective residue homomorphism $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal, a map $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ on places, together with the requirements that an element of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ be integral exactly when it lies in $A$, that the residue map be compatible with the residue map of $A$, that every nonzero element be scalable into the integers with nonzero residue, and that $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ preserve degrees and transport divisors of functions to divisors of their residues. The hypothesis `hR₀` asserts that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\bar{\mathbb Q}((t))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, viewed as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **The local base field.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$; write $A_0 := A \cap k_0$ for the valuation subring `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`, and $\kappa_0$ for its residue field. An element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$, and hypotheses: $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), $A_0$ is Henselian local (`hhens`), $\kappa_0$ is algebraically closed (`hres`), and every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hκ`).
--
--   **Roots of unity and the level structure.** An element $\xi \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell_g$-th root of unity (`hξ`), with the normalisation `hιξ` that some ring homomorphism $k_0 \to \mathbb C$ carries $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell_g))$; write $\zeta$ for the corresponding unit of $k_0$. A subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ which, by `hH₁`, is the intersection of `levelH q M'` with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$. An intermediate field $K$ of $k_0((t))/k_0$ which, by `hK`, is the $k_0$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images of the $\mathbb Q$-function field `xHFunctionField (q^2 * M') H₁`, together with an $A_0$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $k_0$. An element $j \in K$ whose underlying Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of `jq`, assumed nonzero.
--
--   **Functoriality hypotheses for the rigid data.** For every $A_0$-algebra $T$: `hℓ` requires that `IsGamma1Point W ℓg D` (the affine equation at $(x_P,y_P)$, vanishing of $(W.\mathrm{preΨ}\,\ell_g)$ at $x_P$, and $x_Q = x_P$, $y_Q = y_P$) be preserved by a variable change $C$ applied to $W$ and to $D$; `hM` requires `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` to be preserved, the polynomial being replaced by `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h`; `hL` requires that $h \mid \mathrm{inLineMulPoly}\,W\,\ell_g\,n\,x$ imply `kernelVariableChangeDeg C d h` $\mid \mathrm{inLineMulPoly}\,(C \bullet W)\,\ell_g\,n\,(u^{-2}(x-r))$. Further: a family of group laws $\mathcal G$ on $A_0$-algebras which is chord–tangent (`h𝒢`) and has the origin as identity (`h𝒢O`); a `LevelTransport` $\mathcal T$ for $\mathcal G$ at $q$ which is a section transport (`h𝒯`); the hypotheses `hVC` and `hCO` providing, for every projective Weierstrass curve over an $A_0$-algebra, graded ring homomorphisms on the graded coordinate rings realising respectively a variable change (`IsVariableChangeHom`) and a coefficient homomorphism (`IsCoefficientHom`), each compatible with the irrelevant ideals. These data determine the rigid Weierstrass datum `rigidDataH1Pow A₀ ℓg M' q hℓ hM hL 𝒢 𝒯`, whose level object is a triple consisting of kernel polynomials at the prime powers dividing $M'$, a `LevelPData` for $\ell_g$, and a Drinfeld pair at $q$; write $D$ for the associated `LevelModuliDatum`.
--
--   **Moduli package and the Tate point.** A representing package $P_0$ for $D$ over $A_0$: an $A_0$-algebra $P_0.B_0$ with a universal point $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ through which every $D$-point of every $A_0$-algebra factors uniquely. A point $x_0 \in D.\mathrm{Pt}\,K$ whose $j$-invariant `jOf x₀`, read in $k_0((t))$, equals `jqNModC k₀ q` (`hx₀`). An $A_0$-algebra homomorphism $\mathrm{clC}$ from $P_0.B_0$ to the chart subalgebra `chartAlgFin A₀ K j` of $K$, whose composition with the inclusion into $K$ is the classifying map $P_0.\mathrm{classify}\ x_0$ (`hclC`).
--
--   **The pinning hypothesis `hμ`.** There exist a variable change $C$ over $k_0((t))$ and a raw point $r$ of the rigid datum over $K$ such that: the class of $r$ in $D.\mathrm{Pt}\,K$ is $x_0$; writing $(x_\zeta,y_\zeta) := \mathrm{tateToricPoint}\,k_0\,q\,(\zeta^{q})$, the coefficients of $C$ satisfy $u\,(2x_\zeta + 1/6) = 2y_\zeta + x_\zeta$, $C.r = -1/12$, $C.s = -1/2$, $C.t = 1/24$ (the last three as constant Laurent series); the base change of $r.\mathrm{curve}$ to $k_0((t))$ is $C \bullet \mathrm{tateBase}\,k_0\,q$; for every prime factor $p$ of $M'$, every field $F'$ with a ring homomorphism $f : k_0 \to F'$ and every primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta' \in F'$, the image of the $p$-component $r.\mathrm{level}.1\,p$ in $F'((t))$ equals `kernelVariableChangeDeg` of $C$ along $f$, of degree `gamma0PowDeg p (M'.factorization p)`, applied to $\prod_{a}\bigl(X - (\mathrm{toricPoint}\,F'\,q\,(\zeta'^a))_1\bigr)$, the product being over $1 \le a \le p^{v_p(M')}/2$ with $p \nmid a$; the image of $r.\mathrm{level}.2.1$ in $k_0((t))$ is the $C$-variable change of the `LevelPData` $(x_\zeta, y_\zeta, x_\zeta, y_\zeta)$; and there exist $P_x, P_y, Q_x, Q_y \in K$ whose images in $k_0((t))$ are the four coordinates of $(\mathrm{cuspData}\,k_0\,q\,(\zeta^{\ell_g})\,(1,0)\,(0,-1)).\mathrm{variableChange}\,C$ and such that `IsSectionThrough` holds for the sections $P$ and $Q$ of $r.\mathrm{level}.2.2$ through $(P_x,P_y)$ and $(Q_x,Q_y)$ respectively.
--
--   **Compatibility of residue fields.** A ring homomorphism $\theta : \kappa_0 \to \kappa$ with $\theta(\mathrm{residue}_{A_0}(a)) = \mathrm{residue}_A(a)$ for every $a \in A_0$, the right-hand side taken along $A_0 \subseteq A$ (`hθ`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a map
--   $$\Phi : \mathrm{ModuliPoint}\,M'\,\kappa_0 \longrightarrow \mathrm{Place}\,\kappa\,(\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'),$$
--   from the quotient of the pairs (elliptic curve over $\kappa_0$, point of exact order $M'$) by the relation generated by `Gamma0Pair.Step`, such that $\Phi$ is injective and the following holds.
--
--   Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of `chartAlgFin A₀ K j` and $\psi$ an $A_0$-algebra homomorphism from that chart algebra to $\kappa_0$ whose vanishing locus is exactly $y$ (for all $c$, $\psi(c) = 0$ iff $c \in y$). Let $x$ be a raw point of the rigid datum over $\kappa_0$ whose class in the point set over $\kappa_0$ is the image of $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ under $\psi \circ \mathrm{clC}$. Assume that $x.\mathrm{curve}$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion over $\kappa_0$, i.e. $q \cdot P = 0$ implies $P = 0$ for every affine point $P$. Let $g$ be an affine point of $x.\mathrm{curve}$ satisfying the hypothesis `hg`, namely that $g$ has exact order $M'$ and that for every prime factor $p$ of $M'$, every $n$ and every nonsingular point $(x_1,y_1)$ with $n \cdot g = (x_1,y_1)$ and $n \cdot g$ of exact order $p^{v_p(M')}$, the element $x_1$ is a root of the polynomial $x.\mathrm{level}.1\,p$. Let $r$ be a place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$ over $\kappa$ which is rational (the structure map $\kappa \to r.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ is surjective) and whose valuation subring contains $\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,\kappa\,M'$. Assume finally the comparison hypothesis: for every Laurent series $g_f$ over $\mathbb Q$ belonging to `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, which has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ at which the image of `jq` has non-negative order, and whose coefficientwise image over $k_0$ lies in $K$ and in the chart algebra, one has that the $R_0$-residue of $g_f$ lies in the valuation subring of $r$ and that $\theta(\psi(g_f))$ equals $r.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue.
--
--   Then $r = \Phi$ of the class of the pair $\langle x.\mathrm{curve},\ \text{ellipticity from } x.\mathrm{isUnit}\Delta,\ g,\ \text{exact order } M'\rangle$ in $\mathrm{ModuliPoint}\,M'\,\kappa_0$, and $r$ lies in `ssPlaces q M' κ`.
--
--   This is the level-$H_1$ form of the dictionary between $\kappa_0$-points of the chart of the modular curve attached to $H_1 \le (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ and supersingular places of the level-$M'$ modular function field in characteristic $q$: each such point with no nonzero $q$-torsion and a point of exact order $M'$ determines, through an injective assignment on $\Gamma_0(M')$-moduli classes, the place read off by the prescribed evaluations. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.moduliPoint_mk_eq_of_forall_apply_eq_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataH1Pow_of_tatePoint_pinGamma1`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.moduliPoint_mk_eq_of_forall_apply_eq_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataH1Pow_of_tatePoint_pinGamma1) to identify moduli classes from the places they induce.
